# Functional test: on Ze's kernel, whose K1 receipt carries capability bit 3 (K3's
# fragment guard), a commit that adds a port-scoped bypass for a protected subnet is
# accepted, and the kernel holds the entry's forward decision with its port and its
# forward gate, beside the projections of the start configuration's accepted shapes.
# Spec: spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps (AC-22's bit-3 half,
#       AC-2, AC-16; the projection is documented in
#       docs/architecture/ike/ipsec-8-ikev2-child-xfrm.md, "Transit traffic").
#
# RFC 4301 Section 7.4: "All implementations MUST support stateful fragment checking
# to accommodate BYPASS traffic for which a non-trivial port range is specified."
#
# QUESTION: on a kernel that gathers forwarded fragments, does a port-scoped bypass
# for a protected subnet commit through the real reload pipeline and reach the REAL
# kernel SPD as a forward entry carrying its port? Unit tests decide each half over
# dataplane doubles: TestPortScopedBypassForwardPathFollowsFragmentGathering
# (engine/spd_policy.go spdTransitPolicies), TestRFC4301PortScopedForwardBypassRefusedAtCommit
# (the refusal without bit 3). Only a guest booted on Ze's kernel answers bit 3 from a
# real K1 receipt (dataplane.ForwardFragmentGatherer on the xfrm backend), runs the
# commit verifier (verifyForwardBypass, from the ike plugin's OnConfigVerify) against
# that answer, and reads back what XFRM stored, through
# `show vpn ipsec dataplane policy` (ListPolicies -> policyInfoFromKernel).
#
# VALIDATES:
#   The start configuration holds `all-hosts` (any-port bypass, 198.18.253.0/24 ->
#   198.18.254.0/24), `drop-ssh` (port 22 discard, local 198.18.252.0/24) and `mgmt-ze`
#   (port 22 bypass, local 127.0.0.1/32, an address the host holds). After the start
#   the kernel holds a forward decision for each: all-hosts with no port, drop-ssh as
#   discard on port 22, and mgmt-ze, a port-scoped bypass, on port 22.
#   The reload adds `transit-ssh` (port 22 bypass, local 198.18.250.0/24, remote
#   198.18.251.0/24, direction both by default). The reload is accepted, no refusal is
#   logged, and the kernel holds both halves of its transit projection:
#     - the decision, the in half's selectors in FWD with the entry's action:
#       bypass, fwd, dst 198.18.250.0/24, dst-port 22;
#     - the FWD gate, the out half's selectors in FWD at PriorityTransitGate:
#       bypass, fwd, dst 198.18.251.0/24, dst-port any, and on the same row
#       priority 4294967293 (dataplane.PriorityUnmatched - 2), src 198.18.250.0/24,
#       src-port 22.
#   mgmt-ze's forward decision is still held after the reload.
# PREVENTS: a port-scoped bypass refused, or committed with no forward entry, on the
#   kernel that gathers fragments (RFC 4301 Section 7.4 met by the stateful check, yet
#   forwarded traffic on the bypass port kept the next entry's disposition); a forward
#   entry stored without its port, which would bypass every port.
#
# NO NEGATIVE HERE. The refused shape (a port-scoped bypass for a protected subnet on a
# kernel without bit 3) is not reachable in this guest: every QEMU guest boots Ze's
# kernel with K3, and its receipt carries bit 3. That half is proven by
# TestRFC4301PortScopedForwardBypassRefusedAtCommit and
# TestPortScopedBypassNeverReachesTheForwardPath over dataplane doubles that declare
# no gathering. The RED PROOF below reaches the same refusal by forcing the answer.
#
# WHY A RELOAD AND NOT ONLY A START. A start is never verified and never refuses the
# IPsec block (owner decision 3 (a) of 2026-11-19); only a commit runs
# verifyForwardBypass, so only a reload proves the commit accepts the entry.
#
# WHY THESE PREFIXES. RFC 2544 benchmarking ranges. transit-ssh's remote
# 198.18.251.0/24 is named by no other entry here, so its FWD gate is the only fwd row
# with that destination. The SPD is node-wide, and option=exclusive:group=ipsec-xfrm
# keeps every other real-XFRM test's entries out of it while this one runs.
#
# WHY EACH NEEDLE BINDS ONE ROW. `has` re-encodes the answer as compact JSON, whose map
# keys are sorted: action, direction, dst, dst-port, icmp-error-payload, ..., priority,
# reqid, role, spd, src, src-port, tunnel-dst, tunnel-src, upper-proto. A needle is one
# contiguous run of adjacent keys, so it cannot span two rows. action, direction, dst
# and dst-port are adjacent, and so are priority, reqid, role, spd, src and src-port.
# The in half (direction in) and the OUT gate (direction out) share the decision's
# selectors and do not match its needle; the out half shares the FWD gate's source but
# sits at the entry's order 1004, so it does not match the gate's priority needle.
#
# RED PROOF: in internal/component/ike/engine/spd_policy.go, make spdForwardGathers
# answer false: the start installs mgmt-ze with no forward entry, so the first `has`
# on dst 127.0.0.1/32 fails (LIVE-STAGES line, rejected below); with that step removed,
# the reload is refused naming transit-ssh (the reject on "is a bypass with a port"
# fires) and no FWD entry with dst 198.18.250.0/24 or 198.18.251.0/24 appears.
#
# Gated option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf: the daemon loads the real xfrm backend
# and programs real XFRM policies, so this SKIPs on a host without CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# runs as root in the QEMU guest.

# bpf: the default `vpn ipsec application-override deny` loads a cgroup setsockopt guard.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf
# Serialize against every other real-XFRM ipsec test: the SPD is NODE-WIDE.
option=exclusive:group=ipsec-xfrm
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ze_log_ike:value=info

# The configuration the operator commits: the start configuration plus transit-ssh.
# The plugin block is byte-identical to the start one, so the reload keeps the
# fixture alive.
tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONFIG2
plugin {
	external live-stages {
		run "le test fixture reload/live-stages stages.script"
		encoder json
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy all-hosts {
			action bypass
			order 1001
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 198.18.253.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
		policy drop-ssh {
			action discard
			order 1002
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 198.18.252.0/24
				port 22
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
		policy mgmt-ze {
			action bypass
			order 1003
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 127.0.0.1/32
				port 22
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
		policy transit-ssh {
			action bypass
			order 1004
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 198.18.250.0/24
				port 22
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.251.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG2

# Each `has` polls the command until its compact JSON answer holds the needle (20s
# bound), so every step waits on kernel state, never on time.
tmpfs=stages.script:terminator=EOF_SCRIPT
# The start configuration's forward decisions.
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"bypass","direction":"fwd","dst":"198.18.253.0/24","dst-port":"any"
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"discard","direction":"fwd","dst":"198.18.252.0/24","dst-port":"22"
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"bypass","direction":"fwd","dst":"127.0.0.1/32","dst-port":"22"
reload config2.conf
# transit-ssh's decision: the in half's selectors in FWD, with its port.
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"bypass","direction":"fwd","dst":"198.18.250.0/24","dst-port":"22"
# transit-ssh's FWD gate: the out half's selectors in FWD.
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"bypass","direction":"fwd","dst":"198.18.251.0/24","dst-port":"any"
# The same gate row: PriorityTransitGate, sourced from the bypass's port.
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "priority":4294967293,"reqid":0,"role":"operator","spd":"node","src":"198.18.250.0/24","src-port":"22"
# mgmt-ze's forward decision survived the reload.
has show vpn ipsec dataplane policy => "action":"bypass","direction":"fwd","dst":"127.0.0.1/32","dst-port":"22"
say FORWARD-BYPASS-PROJECTED
EOF_SCRIPT

# ── The daemon (REAL xfrm): the three accepted entries ──
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external live-stages {
		run "le test fixture reload/live-stages stages.script"
		encoder json
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy all-hosts {
			action bypass
			order 1001
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 198.18.253.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
		policy drop-ssh {
			action discard
			order 1002
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 198.18.252.0/24
				port 22
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
		policy mgmt-ze {
			action bypass
			order 1003
			protocol 6
			local {
				prefix 127.0.0.1/32
				port 22
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.254.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# The fixture's last step passes, then it asks the daemon to shut down cleanly.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=85s

expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=FORWARD-BYPASS-PROJECTED
# No refusal at the commit and no Error log at the start (both carry this problem text).
reject=stderr:contains=is a bypass with a port, and Ze cannot apply it to the traffic it forwards
reject=stderr:pattern=could not install operator SPD policy
reject=stderr:pattern=LIVE-STAGES line
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
